---
/* ============================================================================
   Analytics
   ============================================================================
   Foundation, edit with care.

   Cloudflare Web Analytics: privacy-friendly, cookie-free traffic
   measurement. Free at our volume. The beacon script reports page views and
   Web Vitals to Cloudflare's analytics endpoint; no cookie banner needed
   because nothing is stored on the visitor's device.

   Setup:
     1. dash.cloudflare.com > Analytics & Logs > Web Analytics > Add a site
     2. Cloudflare gives you a token (a hex string).
     3. Set PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN in .env locally and in
        Cloudflare Pages > Settings > Build > Variables and secrets.
     4. Push a small commit (or click Retry deployment) so the new build
        bakes the token into the beacon script.

   This component renders nothing if the token is missing, so local dev
   and any preview deploy without the variable stays clean.

   The two script tags live in ./analytics/ (CloudflareBeacon.astro and
   GoogleAnalytics.astro) rather than inline here: prettier-plugin-astro
   cannot parse a <script> nested inside a `{cond && (...)}` expression.
   This file owns the env reading and the conditions; those own the tags.
   ============================================================================ */

import CloudflareBeacon from './analytics/CloudflareBeacon.astro';
import GoogleAnalytics from './analytics/GoogleAnalytics.astro';

// PUBLIC_ prefix is required because the script tag runs in the browser.
// The value is inlined at build time (this is a prerendered layout), so
// the env var must be set on the BUILD environment in Cloudflare, not
// the runtime environment.
const token = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN ?? '';
const hasToken = token.length > 0;

// Google Analytics 4. The GA4 property (www.nixoncreativestudio.com,
// 532519109) went dark in 2026-06 because the Astro rebuild never carried the
// gtag snippet the old site had. PUBLIC_GA_ID is the property's web data
// stream Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX), not the numeric property id. Empty
// means no GA4 at all, same as the beacon above.
const gaId = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_ID ?? '').trim();
const hasGa = /^G-[A-Z0-9]+$/.test(gaId);
---

{hasToken && <CloudflareBeacon token={token} />}
{hasGa && <GoogleAnalytics gaId={gaId} />}
